    "desc": "The Godfather of Soul who fused music, Black pride, and political action — recording 'Say It Loud — I'm Black and I'm Proud' in 1968 and using a televised concert to keep Boston calm the night after Martin Luther King Jr. was assassinated.",
    "question": "<p>Which 1968 James Brown song became an anthem of Black pride and self-determination during the Civil Rights Movement?</p>",
